" -> ","spell attack ","attack "," (a creature it has grabbed)","\nAbilities:\n","\nSpells on its statblock: ","\nYou know little about this creature.\nUse Recall Knowledge (Skills menu) to learn its defences.\n","|r","\n(",")\n\n","Harmful font: 4 extra casts of Harm at your highest rank (5 at 5th level, 6 at 15th), shown as green circles. Only Harm can use them.\nHarm deals void damage to a living creature, basic Fortitude save: 1 action (touch, an enemy within reach, 1d8 per rank), 2 actions (an enemy within 30 feet, 1d8 per rank) or 3 actions (every living enemy, 1d8 per rank). Undead and constructs are unaffected. Harm can\'t heal your living party; you can still prepare Heal in ordinary slots.",
"Healing font: 4 extra casts of Heal at your highest rank (5 at 5th level, 6 at 15th), shown as green circles. Only Heal can use them.\nHeal: 1 action (touch, an ally regains 1d8 HP per rank), 2 actions (1d8 + 8 per rank) or 3 actions (every ally, 1d8 per rank). Against undead it deals 1d8 vitality damage per rank instead (basic Fortitude save); the 3-action version hits every undead enemy while it heals your allies.","Magus|Inexorable Iron","Greatsword. In Arcane Cascade you gain temporary HP equal to half your level as you enter it and at the start of each of your turns. Conflux spell: Thunderous Strike (a Strike, then sonic damage in a 15-foot cone; a critical failure knocks prone).",
"Magus|Laughing Shadow","Rapier, other hand free; Dexterity. In Arcane Cascade, Strikes against off-guard foes deal 3 Cascade damage (5 at 7th, 7 at 15th). Conflux spell: Dimensional Assault (teleport next to any enemy, any row, and Strike).","Magus|Sparkling Targe","Longsword and steel shield (Raise Shield, Shield Block). In Arcane Cascade a raised shield adds its bonus to saves against magic and blocks magical damage too, with Hardness raised by your Cascade resistance. Conflux spell: Shielding Strike (raise the shield and Strike).",
"Magus|Starlit Span","Longbow; Dexterity. Spellstrike with your bow at any range. In Arcane Cascade your arrows ignore the cover the target\'s allies give it (the Cascade damage itself is for melee). Conflux spell: Shooting Star (a shot that ignores cover; a hit leaves a trail so no one\'s attacks against it count cover until your next turn).","Magus|Twisting Tree","A staff that reshapes: two hands d8 with reach (any enemy row) and trip, one hand d6 agile. Conflux spell: Spinning Staff (Strike two different foes; it charges Spellstrike).",
"Magus|Twofold Tine","Longsword and shortsword. In Arcane Cascade, a Strike with one blade raises the other\'s Cascade damage to 2 (4 at 7th, 6 at 15th) for the rest of the turn. Conflux spell: Force Fling (a Strike at a foe up to 15 feet away, any row; all its damage becomes force).","Barbarian|Fury","Greataxe. Rage damage 3 (7 at 7th, 13 at 15th). Raging resistance against physical damage from weapons.","Barbarian|Giant","A greatclub built for a Large creature. Rage damage 6 with it (10 at 7th, 18 at 15th), but you\'re clumsy 1 while raging (-1 AC and Reflex). Raging resistance to bludgeoning and fire.",
"Barbarian|Dragon","Greatsword; a diabolic dragon\'s fire. Rage damage 4 fire (8 at 7th, 16 at 15th). Dragon\'s Rage Breath at 6th: a 30-foot cone of fire, 1d6 per level. Raging resistance to piercing and fire.","Barbarian|Spirit","Maul. Rage damage 3 spirit (7 at 7th, 13 at 15th) when spirit does more than your weapon\'s type would; your Strikes have ghost touch. Raging resistance to void and to undead.","Barbarian|Animal","The bear: jaws 1d10 piercing and claws 1d6 slashing (agile); no weapons. Rage damage 2 (5 at 7th, 12 at 15th) and the dice grow a size at 7th. Raging resistance to piercing and slashing.",
"Barbarian|Superstition","Greataxe. While raging, +2 to saves against magic, and Rage heals you as much as its temporary HP once per fight. Rage damage 3, 4 against creatures you\'ve seen cast a spell. Anathema: allies\' area spells pass you by, and a spell aimed at you makes you frightened 1. Raging resistance to spells.","Fighter|Sword & Board","Longsword and steel shield. Raise Shield (+2 AC) and Shield Block (reaction: reduce physical damage by 5).","Fighter|Two-Hander","A greatsword (d12). Vicious Swing adds weapon dice.",
"Fighter|Duelist","A rapier (finesse). Dueling Parry (+2 AC) and Dual-Handed Assault (bigger damage die).","Fighter|Archer","A longbow (hits any row). Exacting Strike, Double Shot (two targets), Debilitating Shot and Impossible Volley.","Fighter|Dual Weapons","A longsword and a shortsword, one in each hand. Double Slice, Twin Parry (+1 AC) and Two-Weapon Flurry.","Fighter|Polearm","A halberd (d10, reach: hits any row). Lunge, Spear Dancer, and Haft Striker Stance to fight with the haft as a second weapon.",
"Champion|Justice","Retributive Strike: an ally you protect gains resistance 2 + your level and you Strike the enemy if it\'s in reach.","Champion|Redemption","Glimpse of Redemption: an ally you protect gains resistance 2 + your level and the enemy is enfeebled 2.","Champion|Liberation","Liberating Step: an ally you protect gains resistance 2 + your level (and may break free and Step).","Champion|Grandeur","Flash of Grandeur: an ally you protect gains resistance 2 + your level and revealing light dazzles the enemy.",
"Champion|Obedience","Unholy. Iron Command: an enemy that hurts you must kneel (prone) or take mental damage. Touch of the Void instead of Lay on Hands.","Champion|Desecration","Unholy. Selfish Shield: resistance 2 + half your level against an enemy that hurts you. Touch of the Void instead of Lay on Hands.","Champion|Iniquity","Unholy. Destructive Vengeance: take more damage from a blow and deal it back as spirit damage. Touch of the Void instead of Lay on Hands.","Cleric|Cloistered Cleric","No armor; Domain Initiate (fire ray). Expert spellcasting at 7th, master at 15th, legendary at 19th.",
"Cleric|Warpriest","Breastplate, warhammer, Raise Shield and Shield Block. Expert Fortitude; spellcasting expert at 11th.","Ranger|Flurry","Your multiple attack penalty against your prey is -3/-6 (-2/-4 with agile weapons).","Ranger|Precision","Your first hit each round against your prey deals +1d8 precision damage (2d8 at 11th, 3d8 at 19th).","Ranger|Outwit","+2 to Deception, Intimidation and Recall Knowledge against your prey, and +1 AC against its attacks.","Rogue|Ruffian","Strength key attribute, medium armor, and sneak attack with a mace (simple weapons up to d8).",
